GPU&#x2F;CUDA: Yes, but disabled by default for faster builds. To enable: remove LLAMA_CUDA = &quot;OFF&quot; from config.toml and rebuild with CUDA toolkit installed.<p>Rust library: Absolutely! Add shimmy = { version = &quot;0.1.0&quot;, features = [&quot;llama&quot;] } to Cargo.toml. Use the inference engine directly:<p>let engine = shimmy::engine::llama::LlamaEngine::new();
let model = engine.load(&amp;spec).await?;
let response = model.generate(&quot;prompt&quot;, opts, None).await?;<p>No need to spawn processes - just import and use the components directly in your Rust code.
